  "recovery_latency_s": 190.61798429489136,
  "client_view_text": " A message that changes his life forever.\nThe lighthouse keeper, Jack, had been stationed on the rocky coast for five years. He had grown accustomed to the solitude, the rhythmic sound of the waves, and the occasional visit from a passing ship. But on this particular day, something caught his eye. A bottle, half-buried in the sand, caught the morning sun and glinted like a tiny jewel. Jack picked it up, blowing off the sand and examining it. It was an old-fashioned bottle, with a cork stopper and a faded label. He turned it over in his hands, wondering what could be inside.\n\nAs he carefully removed the cork, a piece of paper slipped out, carrying with it a faint scent of saltwater and seaweed. Jack unfolded the paper, and his eyes widened as he read the message scrawled on it:\n\n\"Dear Lighthouse Keeper,\n\nI am writing to you from the other side of the world. I am a sailor, and I have been at sea for months. I have seen the most incredible things - schools of dolphins, bioluminescent fish, and even a whale breaching in the distance. But it is not the sea creatures that I have seen that have changed me. It is"
}